{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":492721,"name":"Gokul Daroji","username":"Gokul_Daroji","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/cdc98d/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T12:11:16.955Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAgent Computer is in a partial state. Windows Grok Bot app and the phone Grok Bot app are both silent. Bots do not reply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWeekly Grok Bot usage is 31% used, reset in about 4 days. This is not a usage-limit issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I already tried:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit from tray and ended leftover Grok Bot processes in Task Manager\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRetry — no connection attempt\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRecover Grok Bot’s Computer — stuck at 75%, then stopped without reconnecting\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReset Grok Bot’s Computer — result: partial state\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease rebuild the Agent Computer on the backend. Bots, files, and logins should be kept.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOperating System\u003cbr\u003e\nWindows (desktop app) and phone Grok Bot app\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion Information\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot Windows: 0.53.0\u003cbr\u003e\nPhone: Android Samsung S24\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTimezone\u003cbr\u003e\nIST, 16 Sep 2026 ~17:30\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccount email\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"mailto:gokul@dinasidirect.com\"\u003egokul@dinasidirect.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot on Windows. Bots do not reply. Phone Grok Bot app on the same account also does not reply.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCheck Settings → Usage. Weekly usage is 31% used, reset in about 4 days.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot from the system tray. End leftover Grok Bot processes in Task Manager. Reopen the app.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eApp shows Retry and Recover Grok Bot’s Computer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick Recover. Progress reaches 75%, then stops without reconnecting.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eQuit again, reopen. Click Retry. No connection attempt. Same Retry / Recover screen returns.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eQuit again, reopen. Settings → Updates → Reset Grok Bot’s Computer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReset finishes with “partial state.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWindows and phone apps still cannot use the Agent Computer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpected: Recover or Reset reconnects the Agent Computer and bots reply to a simple “hello.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eActual: Computer left in partial state. Desktop and phone both silent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion Information\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot Windows: 0.53.0\u003cbr\u003e\nPhone: Android Samsung S24\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok App Version:1.  10.0 (201)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492721-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492721-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T12:11:27.990Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":33,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":165.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171864,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-agent-computer-partial-state-after-reset-windows-and-phone-both-silent","display_username":"Gokul Daroji","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138140,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-agent-computer-partial-state-after-reset-windows-and-phone-both-silent/171864/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":492765,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T12:37:28.795Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. Two different things overlapped here, so I’ll break them down.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBots weren’t replying (roughly 15:00 to 17:00 IST). This was on our side, not your computer. A message sent around 15:01 got stuck in processing, and everything you sent after that (from both Windows and your phone) queued behind it. Around 17:00 the queue cleared on its own, and the backlog was processed around 17:05-17:07, so you may have seen several replies arrive at once. The root cause on our side is already fixed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecover stuck at 75% and partial state on Windows. Your Agent Computer is actually fine. Every Recover and Reset completed successfully for us in under a minute, and your bots, files, and logins are preserved. The issue is that your PC can’t resolve the machine’s network address via hostname lookup on \u003ccode\u003ecursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e, even though \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e opens normally. That points to DNS on your internet connection, and that’s why the app shows partial state even though the rebuild finished. Please don’t press Reset or Recover again. Each click rebuilds the computer again without helping.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry this on Windows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSwitch DNS to public DNS: Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026amp; Internet \u0026gt; Wi-Fi (or Ethernet) \u0026gt; Hardware properties \u0026gt; DNS server assignment \u0026gt; Edit \u0026gt; Manual \u0026gt; enable IPv4 \u0026gt; Preferred DNS \u003ccode\u003e1.1.1.1\u003c/code\u003e, Alternate DNS \u003ccode\u003e8.8.8.8\u003c/code\u003e \u0026gt; Save.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen PowerShell (Start \u0026gt; type PowerShell) and run \u003ccode\u003eipconfig /flushdns\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRight-click the Grok Bot tray icon \u0026gt; Quit, then reopen Grok Bot and wait about a minute.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend “hello” to one of the bots.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor your phone: if it’s on Jio mobile data or the same Wi-Fi, it’ll likely hit the same lookup issue. On Samsung: Settings \u0026gt; Connections \u0026gt; More connection settings \u0026gt; Private DNS \u0026gt; Private DNS provider hostname \u0026gt; enter \u003ccode\u003eone.one.one.one\u003c/code\u003e \u0026gt; Save, then reopen Grok Bot. Alternatively, test once on a different Wi-Fi or via hotspot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if the bot replies after step 4. If it still won’t connect after changing DNS, send your Grok Bot version from Settings and we’ll dig deeper.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T12:37:28.795Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171864,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-agent-computer-partial-state-after-reset-windows-and-phone-both-silent","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-agent-computer-partial-state-after-reset-windows-and-phone-both-silent/171864/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[492721,492765]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":373,"name":"computer-use","slug":"computer-use"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot Agent Computer partial state after Reset — Windows and phone both silent","id":171864,"title":"Grok Bot Agent Computer partial state after Reset — Windows and phone both silent","posts_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:11:16.924Z","views":38,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-16T12:37:28.795Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"grok-bot-agent-computer-partial-state-after-reset-windows-and-phone-both-silent","category_id":6,"word_count":697,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":138140,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":null,"slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_171864","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":5,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":7,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false}],"chunk_size":20,"bookmarked":false,"topic_timer":{"id":32783,"execute_at":"2026-10-16T12:37:28.795Z","duration_minutes":43200,"based_on_last_post":true,"status_type":"close","category_id":null},"message_bus_last_id":17,"participant_count":2,"show_read_indicator":false,"thumbnails":null,"slow_mode_enabled_until":null,"tags_disable_ads":false,"related_topics":[{"fancy_title":"Can\u0026rsquo;t reach your computer, Reset fails - New user","id":171796,"title":"Can't reach your computer, Reset fails - New us